# Contributing

Thanks for helping. This workspace is an Nx monorepo built with nx-polystack; the steps below keep
every app and library consistent.

## Branches and pull requests

1. Branch from `<%= baseBranch %>`: `feature-<ticket>` (for example `feature-ABC-123`).
2. Keep each pull request small and focused on one ticket.
3. Open the pull request against `<%= baseBranch %>`. CI must pass and a reviewer must approve
   before it is merged.

## Commit messages

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) with the ticket as the scope:

```text
feat(<ticket>): add the order summary page
fix(<ticket>): keep the session after a token refresh
docs(<ticket>): explain the release steps
```

Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`, `ci`, `perf`. Commit messages
are checked by commitlint on commit, and pull request titles are checked in CI.

## Adding apps, libraries and environments

Use the generators so tags, tsconfig paths and npm scripts stay consistent:

```bash
pstack app --type=<angular|ionic|flutter> --name=<name>
pstack lib --type=<type> --name=<name>
pstack env --name=<env>
pstack llm      # refresh the generated block in the AI-assistant files
```

## Before you push

```bash
npm run lint                               # lint the workspace
npx nx affected -t lint typecheck test build   # lint, type-check, test and build what changed
npm run check:cycles                       # fail on new project dependency cycles
npm run stale-code                         # report unused files, exports and dependencies
```

The pre-push hook runs `npm run check:prepush`: a secret scan that blocks the push, then a
dependency audit that only warns. Run `npm run check:audit` for the strict audit (it fails on
high or critical advisories).

## Pull request checklist

- [ ] The title follows Conventional Commits, with the ticket as the scope.
- [ ] Lint, tests and build pass.
- [ ] No secrets, keys or plaintext environment values are committed.
- [ ] Docs are updated when behaviour changes.
- [ ] UI changes include screenshots.

